        <div class="zx-order">
          <div class="zx-order-top"><span class="zx-pill zx-pill-green">Option A</span> NSM Hosting</div>
          <h3>We host it for you</h3>
          <p>Create and manage your server through the NSM Hosting dashboard &mdash; the official server files are installed automatically, ports are assigned, and the console, files, backups and support live in one browser tab. Free forever, no payment required.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:14px">
            <a class="btn primary" href="/hosting" data-no-spa="1">Open NSM Hosting</a>
            <a class="btn" href="/hosting/create" data-no-spa="1">Deploy a server</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="zx-order">
          <div class="zx-order-top"><span class="zx-pill zx-pill-dark">Option B</span> Self-Hosted NSM Server</div>
          <h3>Host it yourself</h3>
          <p>Download the official NSM server files and run the server on your own computer or VPS machine. The package includes the server, its configuration, the resources it needs and a setup readme.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:14px 0 6px">
            <a class="btn primary" href="/download/server" data-no-spa="1">&#11015; Download NSM Server</a>
          </div>
          <ol style="margin:10px 0 0;padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7">
            <li>Download and extract <strong>NSM-Server.zip</strong> on the machine that will run it.</li>
            <li>Run <strong>START-SERVER.bat</strong> (Windows) &mdash; it installs the runtime and starts the server; <strong>readme-server.txt</strong> covers Linux and advanced setup.</li>
            <li>Edit <strong>server.cfg</strong> to name your city, then open the ports listed in the readme so players can join.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

